Now I have comprehensive data for my review. Let me synthesize everything into a final assessment.

**Summary of independent verification:**

**References verified:** ✅ The Verifier Tax (2603.19328), ✅ BackBench (2604.18847), ✅ AIR (2602.11749), ✅ ReGuard (2510.13727), ✅ ToolMisuseBench (2604.01508), ✅ GTPO (2511.14846), ✅ AT²PO (2601.04767), ✅ GAGPO (2605.13217), ✅ Fission-GRPO (2601.15625), ✅ Canonical Path Deviation (2602.19008), ✅ ToolSafe (2601.10156), ✅ RAC (2605.03409), ✅ SafePred, ✅ T2PO (ICML 2026 Spotlight), ✅ RC-GRPO (2602.03025), ✅ Qwen3.6-35B-A3B confirmed real

**Venue deadlines verified:** ✅ EACL 2027 ARR Aug 3, commitment Oct 11 ✅ AAAI 2027 abstract Jul 21, paper Jul 28

**Cost verified:** H100 spot at ~$1.03-$2.50/hr, $2/hr estimate is realistic

**Critical finding — missing paper:** "Symbolic Guardrails for Domain-Specific Agents" (arXiv 2604.15579, April 2026) directly evaluates post-blocking behavior on tau²-bench and finds guardrails **improve** pass rates (GPT-4o: 0.36→0.48, GPT-5: 0.68→0.70), with the authors stating agents "use blocking feedback to adjust actions, retry with a safer alternative, and often complete the task successfully."

